intensifier), and a few translated excess adverbs. Short fragments ending
in oo/aa also get negative values; a single vowel extending the preceding
vowel gets a stronger one. Closing such a pair with consonants usually
weakens or reverses that response. Ordinary longer words stay near zero.
Repeated middle dots, initial 'o', and initial 'Title:' are secondary cues.
Only a short text tail is carried, reset at document boundaries.
"""
import re
import string

READS = ()
BE = {'am', 'is', 'are', 'was', 'were', 'be', "'s"}
INTENSIFIERS = {'far', 'way', 'much'}
